TITLE:: REOfflineTap
summary:: A rig's SendReply tap written into a buffer in an offline render
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REOfflineClock, Classes/RCVisuals, Classes/REVisualsTape, Classes/RERenderedPlayer

DESCRIPTION::
In a take rendered offline (HomewareSC's code::scripts/take.sh render::, an link::Classes/REOfflineClock:: and an code::RECollectAddr::) scsynth NRT answers no reply, so what a rig's tap synth sends to the language live with link::Classes/SendReply:: (the positions and levels link::Classes/RCVisuals#*relay:: forwards to HomewareVisuals as code::/lsys/state:: or code::/orgnsm/state::) never arrives. An REOfflineTap stands in for such a tap: the SynthDef's offline variant writes the same values into a Buffer at the tap's rate (link::#*record::), the render writes every buffer to a float sound file at its end (link::#*writeLines::), and HomewareSC's code::scripts/analysis/hwa/viztape.py:: turns the frames into entries of the visuals tape, code::<take>.viz.json:: (link::Classes/REVisualsTape::).

Frame code::i:: of a tap's buffer is code::[i + 1] ++ values:: latched at trigger code::i:: (time code::i / rate:: from the synth's start): channel 0 stays 0 on a frame never written (a tap freed before the end of the render), and the frames of a tap that outlives its buffer all land on the last frame, whose counter then exceeds its index (the reader reports the overflow). The buffer is sized from link::#*endSecs:: (the clock seconds the render ends at, set by the render) and the clock's seconds when the tap is made. A tap's creation time is read back from the collected bundles by its node id: the rig writes no sidecar. Nothing here reaches a live server: link::#*new:: refuses one.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: server
The offline server: its address, followed through the code::BundleNetAddr:: of a code::server.bind::, must be an code::RECollectAddr::.
argument:: defName
The offline variant of the tap's SynthDef, built on link::#*record::.
argument:: key
The rig's key (code::\lsys::, code::\plankton::), in the file name.
argument:: path
The address of the tape entries (code::'/lsys/state'::).
argument:: head
The arguments that lead the values in every entry (the first slot the tap covers, as the live tap's replyID).
argument:: rate
Frames per second, capped by link::#*maxRate::.
argument:: numValues
How many values the tap writes per frame (the live tap's values).

METHOD:: record
The UGen graph of a tap's offline variant, in a SynthDef with a code::bufnum:: control.
argument:: bufnum
argument:: rate
argument:: values
An Array of control-rate UGens, the values the live tap sends.

METHOD:: isOffline
True when the server's address is an code::RECollectAddr:: (behind a bind's code::BundleNetAddr::).
METHOD:: collector
That address, nil live.

METHOD:: endSecs
The clock seconds the render ends at: the render sets it before the piece makes its taps (a cap before the take's start is known, the exact end once it is).
METHOD:: defaultSecs
The seconds of frames assumed, with a warning, when endSecs is unset.
METHOD:: maxRate
A cap on every tap's rate (nil: none): HomewareSC's code::take.sh render --state-rate::.

METHOD:: writeLines
The Score lines writing every tap of the server, and the index the merge reads.
argument:: server
argument:: bundles
The collected bundles (code::RECollectAddr.bundles::): each tap's code::/s_new:: is found there by node id. A tap never sent is left out, with a warning.
argument:: folder
The folder of the sound files.
argument:: atTime
The score time of the writes (the end of the render).
argument:: startSecs
The take's start on the clock: the index's code::t0:: is in tape time, seconds from the take's start.
returns:: An Event: code::lines:: (code::[atTime, ['/b_write', ...]]:: per tap sent) and code::index:: (per tap: code::key::, code::path::, code::head::, code::file::, code::rate::, code::values::, code::t0::, code::frames::, code::nodeID::, code::createdAt::).

METHOD:: taps
The taps registered for a server.
METHOD:: clear
Forgets a server's taps (every server's when nil).

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: msgs
The code::/b_alloc:: (four arguments: no completion message, which a Score line could not hold) and the synth's code::/s_new:: with its code::bufnum:: appended to code::args::, for the rig's own transport, in one bundle in that order.
argument:: target
argument:: args
argument:: addAction

METHOD:: synth
The tap's Synth (code::basicNew::): the rig keeps it where it keeps the live tap and frees it the same way.
METHOD:: allocMsg
METHOD:: startSecsIn
The seconds of this tap's code::/s_new:: in the collected bundles, nil when it was never sent.
METHOD:: fileName
code::<key>_<head>_<nodeID>.wav::
METHOD:: frames
METHOD:: numChannels
code::numValues + 1::: the counter, then the values.
METHOD:: buffer
METHOD:: bufnum
METHOD:: rate
METHOD:: createdAt
The clock's seconds when the tap was made.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// the rig's def block: the live tap and its offline variant
SynthDef(\LSystem_VizTap_w0_32, { |posBus = 0, levelBus = 0, rate = 20, replyID = 0|
	SendReply.kr(Impulse.kr(rate), '/lsys/viz', In.kr(posBus, 96) ++ In.kr(levelBus, 32), replyID);
}).add;
SynthDef(\LSystem_VizTapBuf_w0_32, { |posBus = 0, levelBus = 0, rate = 20, bufnum = 0|
	REOfflineTap.record(bufnum, rate, In.kr(posBus, 96) ++ In.kr(levelBus, 32));
}).add;

// where the rig makes a tap, in a render (~rc_offline set by take_render.scd)
(
var args = [\posBus, rig.pos_bus.index, \levelBus, rig.level_bus.index, \rate, 20];
if(~rc_offline.notNil) {
	var tap = REOfflineTap(rig.server, \LSystem_VizTapBuf_w0_32, \lsys, '/lsys/state', [0], 20, 128);
	~lsys_send.(tap.msgs(rig.group_lsys, args));
	rig.viz_taps[0] = tap.synth;
} {
	var synth = Synth.basicNew(\LSystem_VizTap_w0_32, rig.server);
	~lsys_send.(synth.newMsg(rig.group_lsys, args ++ [\replyID, 0], \addToTail));
	rig.viz_taps[0] = synth;
};
)

// the render, once the clock ran: the writes at the end of the score, the index next to the files
w = REOfflineTap.writeLines(server, addr.bundles, out ++ ".state", dur, startSecs);
w[\lines].do { |l| score.add(l) };
::
